standup.prompt:
Summarize project progress since the last workday as a standup digest:
1. Use git log to review all commits since the last workday and group changes by module;
2. Check CI status and the latest test run, flagging failures;
3. List pending work and blockers (from TODO markers and unfinished branches).
Output at most 6 bullets, one sentence each, referencing related commits or issues. Read-only analysis — do not modify any code or configuration.

risk_scan.prompt:
Run a risk scan over the last 24 hours of changes:
1. Use git log/diff to collect changes from the last 24 hours (adds, edits, deletions, and config changes);
2. Identify high-risk issues: runtime errors, data loss, permission bypasses, resource leaks, and cross-platform compatibility problems;
3. For each finding give: file path and line, severity (high/medium/low), root cause, and a fix suggestion.
If nothing was found, state clearly that no high-risk changes were detected. Read-only analysis — do not modify code.

release_notes.prompt:
Draft this week's release notes:
1. Use git log to collect this week's merged PRs and commits (diff against the previous release tag if tags exist);
2. Group them into Features / Fixes / UX improvements / Engineering improvements;
3. Produce two drafts: a detailed team version (with PR/commit references) and a concise user-facing version (no internal details).
Read-only analysis — do not modify code.

doc_sync.prompt:
Run a documentation sync check:
1. Collect code, config, and API changes from the last 7 days (git log/diff);
2. Compare them against README, the docs/ directory, and key interface comments to verify docs still match actual behavior;
3. List high-confidence discrepancies where behavior changed but docs were not updated, each with: changed file path, doc location to update, and a concrete update suggestion.
Read-only analysis — do not modify code or docs.
